<div class="page-title">🗺️ <span class="page-title-text">Entity-Relationship Diagram — <%= dataset.dataset_name %></span></div>
<p class="page-subtitle">
  <a href="/browse-dataset" style="color: var(--accent);">← All datasets</a>
  &nbsp;·&nbsp; Dataset ID: <strong><%= dataset.dataset_id %></strong>
</p>
<div class="info-box" style="margin-bottom:18px;">
  Every box below is one uploaded file, and every line is a relationship CMA-FLOW actually confirmed by
  measuring how much two columns' real values overlap — not a guess from column names alone (the same
  detection behind Full Descriptive Analytics' relationship table). Primary/foreign keys and cardinality
  (one-to-one, one-to-many, many-to-many) are read directly off each column's own uniqueness, so this
  diagram regenerates automatically whenever this dataset's files change — nothing here is drawn by hand,
  and no AI model guesses the structure.
</div>

<% if (!erd.mermaid) { %>
  <div class="placeholder-card">
    <div class="emoji">📭</div>
    <p>This dataset has no uploaded files yet. <a href="/upload-dataset" style="color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600;">Upload files</a> to this dataset to see its diagram here.</p>
  </div>
<% } else { %>

  <div class="chart-card">
    <div class="chart-title">
      <%= erd.entityCount %> file<%= erd.entityCount === 1 ? '' : 's' %>
      <% if (erd.relationshipCount > 0) { %>
        · <%= erd.relationshipCount %> relationship<%= erd.relationshipCount === 1 ? '' : 's' %> detected
      <% } %>
    </div>
    <div class="chart-subtitle">
      <strong>PK</strong> = primary key (values never repeat in that file) · <strong>FK</strong> = foreign key
      (the "many" side of a detected relationship) · <code>||</code> = exactly one · <code>o{</code> = many ·
      each relationship line is labeled with its measured value-overlap percentage.
    </div>
    <% if (erd.relationshipCount === 0 && erd.entityCount > 1) { %>
      <p class="chart-subtitle" style="margin-top:-4px;">
        No relationship cleared the minimum confidence overlap between any two of this dataset's files yet —
        the boxes below still show every file's own fields.
      </p>
    <% } %>

    <div id="erd-container" style="overflow:auto; margin-top: 14px; min-height: 120px;">
      <div id="erd-loading" style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 13px;">Rendering diagram…</div>
      <div id="erd-error" class="placeholder-card" hidden>
        <div class="emoji">⚠️</div>
        <p>The diagram couldn't be rendered. The raw definition is below if you'd like to check it yourself.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <details class="chart-table-toggle" style="margin-top: 14px;">
      <summary>Diagram source (Mermaid ER syntax)</summary>
      <pre style="white-space: pre-wrap; font-size: 12px; background: var(--btn-ghost-bg); padding: 10px; border-radius: 8px; overflow:auto;"><%= erd.mermaid %></pre>
    </details>
  </div>

  <script src="/vendor/mermaid.min.js"></script>
  <script>
    (function () {
      var definition = <%- JSON.stringify(erd.mermaid) %>;
      var container = document.getElementById('erd-container');
      var loading = document.getElementById('erd-loading');
      var errorBox = document.getElementById('erd-error');

      if (typeof mermaid === 'undefined') {
        loading.hidden = true;
        errorBox.hidden = false;
        return;
      }

      mermaid.initialize({ startOnLoad: false, theme: 'neutral', securityLevel: 'strict' });

      mermaid.render('erd-diagram-svg', definition)
        .then(function (out) {
          loading.remove();
          var wrap = document.createElement('div');
          wrap.innerHTML = out.svg;
          container.appendChild(wrap);
        })
        .catch(function () {
          loading.hidden = true;
          errorBox.hidden = false;
        });
    })();
  </script>

<% } %>
